## 🧠 Logic Highlights (important lines explained)

| Code Part | What it Does | Why Important |
|------------|----------------|----------------|
| `struct TreeNode { ... };` | Defines node structure | Core of any tree — stores value + left/right pointers |
| `insertNode()` | Recursively adds new node in sorted BST position | Maintains BST property |
| `deleteNode()` | Removes node and restructures tree correctly | Handles 3 cases (no child, one child, two children) |
| `findMin()` | Finds smallest value node | Needed for deletion (inorder successor) |
| `inorder()` | Left → Root → Right traversal | Prints BST in sorted order |
| `height()` | Returns max depth | Good for understanding recursion |
| `freeTree()` | Frees all nodes recursively | Prevents memory leaks |
| Menu loop | Infinite loop with choices | Lets user interactively test all operations |

