Let’s take the **Binary Search Tree (BST) Menu Program** and expand it with **line-by-line comments** + **deep explanations of recursion flow** so you understand not just *what* the code does, but *how the logic flows* during recursive calls.

We’ll keep the same operations (Insert, Delete, Search, Traversals, etc.), but I’ll annotate it heavily — this will be long and extremely clear.  

