# 🧭 FLOW SUMMARY — HOW RECURSION BEHAVES INTERNALLY

| Operation | Recursion Role | Flow |
|------------|----------------|------|
| **Insert** | Finds correct position for new node | Each call goes deeper until `NULL`, creates node, and unwinds returning updated subtree links |
| **Delete** | Finds node to delete and rebuilds structure | Traverses down, modifies child pointer, and returns updated subtree up the chain |
| **Traversal** | Processes nodes in specific sequence | Each recursive call processes subtrees first, then current node (or vice versa) |
| **Height** | Aggregates max depth bottom-up | Leaf returns 1, parent adds +1 each return up the recursion chain |

